{{also|persécuté|persécute}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=follow}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|persécuter}}, from {{der|en|EL.|persecutor}}, from {{der|en|la|persequor|persequor, persecutus|follow up, pursue}}, from {{prefix|la|per|sequor|t1=through|t2=follow|nocat=1}} (English {{m|en|sequel}}). Compare {{m|en|prosecute}}. Cf. also {{m|en|pursue}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɝsəkjut/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpəːsɪkjuːt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-persecute.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To maliciously afflict, annoy, grieve, harm, harass, hunt down, injure, mistreat, oppress, prey upon, or pursue an individual being or groups; usually the object and focus of persecution is contrived to deserve or merit the maltreatment, based upon some perceived petty to existential scaled difference, distinction or status; a grievance, retribution, rivalry, ideological biases: [ abc-xyz ] ability, age, appearance, attire, beliefs, beauty, clan, class, dress, ethnicity, gender, geniture, ... xenophobia, zoology.  
#: {{ux|en|He who '''persecutes''' one will '''persecute''' all.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Matthew|chapter=5|verse=44|passage="Do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and '''persecute''' you."}}
#* {{RQ:Foxe Actes and Monuments}}
#*: I have heard, brethren, how sharply Antichrist '''persecuteth''' you, in vexing the faithful servants of Christ with divers and strange kinds of afflictions.
# To harass with [[importunity]]; to pursue with persistent [[solicitation]]s; to annoy.

